# netsurf: a batch of more than 128 marks coalesces its body marks under their common ancestor (patch 464)
# Generated 2026-11-26
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 463)
#
# A batch with more distinct marks than the extra[] ring holds (128) went
# to the full rebuild unconditionally ("over": wpblog and github, 2.0 a
# load in the 463 census). A probe showed every mark in the document,
# github's body marks meeting at a <div> 4 levels deep or a <tbody> 29
# deep, wpblog's only at <body>. On overflow (macos9_reconvert_coalesce)
# the body marks are replaced by one mark on their lowest common ancestor
# (html_rl_lca) when that is below <body> (html_rl_too_wide); an attribute,
# class or style mark on the ancestor itself could reach its later
# siblings through a + / ~ rule, so the ancestor then goes one level up.
# Head marks stay ordinary extras (compacted in place, the old primary
# appended after them). Later marks inside the subtree are covered; marks
# outside it are ordinary extras again (the slot has room); a second
# overflow coalesces everything then. The coalesced primary is answered by
# html_rl_subtree_rebuild: the local path's prelude, the removed sheets
# pruned, the nearest block, flex or grid box at or above the ancestor
# built again whole (440 / 438) with its own checks, and only then the
# sheet-removal walk (before, it met the batch's new elements without
# boxes); the cost guard still decides. Logged: "LIFE over: N marks coalesced under <x> ..." / "too
# wide to coalesce".
#
